        "id": "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469",
        "title": "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "e9313cab-cba9-5cd5-8159-89c8f05fb6e6",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-27-topic-audit-2/group-3/relocation-assets/17592186087839/a/e03e93ec2a0868287a2769e3fd7fc3927bc23cd0195b51673455a4a6a916a1f6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=9$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{9}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "e9bfa8b2-feec-5e2e-8bdc-1839a09cf704",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
